{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"ade1deb5","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006269,"end_time":"2026-09-30T09:11:31.168608+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T09:11:31.162339+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Refinement patch note — approval boundaries and validation\n","- Implemented only embargo-aligned pooled bootstrap, all-development frozen refit, and deterministic input/code/version provenance. Pooled counts sum every aligned finite-scored embargoed fold/cohort mask, including folds individually skipped for minimum rows/positives; their counts are exported in `aligned_rows_by_fold`.\n","- **Deferred pending approval:** timestamp-history semantics (including tie handling), and replacing the `seed_prior` / `stage2_prob_filled` policy. `build_relational_features`, `audit_relational_causality` and `assert_causal` are unchanged.\n","- Frozen calibration is fitted on selection-model held-out stopping scores before refitting all development rows at fixed selected rounds. Its transfer to the refitted model is **not revalidated**; no OOT labels enter fitting, round selection or calibration.\n","- No training rerun; patched metrics are not verified. Old outputs, counts and execution/papermill metadata were cleared. Focused toy checks validate mechanics (LightGBM stubs, not training results). The proposed slice-0 label-invariance test was **not claimed or passed**: models legitimately train on those labels; the unapproved fill-policy change remains deferred.\n","- In notebooks without `__file__`, `script_sha256` is null. `notebook_code_sha256` is an independently validated build-time code-source snapshot using the exact canonical scope in the dedicated excluded fingerprint cell. Recompute it after editing code. Input hashes snapshot actual bytes read; rejected Stage-1 schema inputs retain their hash with `read_schema_rejected` status.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"51ad61ff","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T09:11:31.181816Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T09:11:31.181294Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.664409Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.663116Z"},"papermill":{"duration":7.493183,"end_time":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.666832+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T09:11:31.173649+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["\"\"\"\n","Stage 2: Graph-Augmented GBDT — Relational Features & Hypothesis Testing\n","========================================================================\n","(Audit-Hardened Edition, v2 — protocol-aligned with Stage 1 v2)\n","\n","Purpose\n","-------\n","(a) Test whether time-causal relational/entity-history features add signal over a\n","    purely tabular GBDT baseline, under a temporally honest protocol; and\n","(b) emit a leakage-free `stage2_prob` representation for the downstream joint\n","    graph-tabular model, with full block coverage including the sealed OOT block.\n","\n","Changes vs. Stage 2 v1 (and why each matters)\n","---------------------------------------------\n"," 1. LIGHTGBM BAGGING BUG FIX. v1 set `subsample: 0.8` with no `bagging_freq`,\n","    so row subsampling was INERT — the reported v1 numbers came from an\n","    unregularised model. Now `bagging_fraction` + `bagging_freq: 1`. This alone\n","    changes the results; v1 Stage 2 metrics must not be quoted.\n"," 2. INTERNAL `base_only` ARM. v1 tested H1 by comparing this notebook's AP\n","    against a *separately executed* Stage 1 run. That confounds \"relational\n","    features help\" with \"different run, different seeds, different round\n","    schedule\". A base-feature-only variant now runs inside this script under\n","    identical folds, seeds, params and embargo, giving a valid paired control.\n","    Cross-stage comparison is retained as a secondary, clearly-labelled check.\n"," 3. EVALUATION vs. FEATURE-GENERATION are separated into two passes, exactly as\n","    in Stage 1 v2. Pass A is embargoed (honest metrics); Pass B scores full\n","    blocks (complete coverage for Stage 3). v1 conflated them, losing ~3% of\n","    Blocks 2-4 and 100% of Block 5.\n"," 4. BLOCK 5 IS NOW SCORED by a frozen model fit on Blocks 1-4. v1 left Block 5\n","    with zero Stage-2 coverage, making the final OOT joint-model comparison\n","    impossible. The Block 5 *target* is never read; enforced by assertion.\n"," 5. BLOCK 1 uses expanding chronological sub-folds (K=4, coverage 75%) instead\n","    of a single half-split (50%), and each sub-fold selects its own boosting\n","    rounds. v1 reused `mean(best_iters_real)` — rounds chosen by folds that had\n","    themselves trained on Block 1.\n"," 6. MULTIPLICITY CONTROL. v1 ran H1/H1a/H1b/N1 across 4 scopes each (up to 16\n","    dependent bootstrap tests) and declared \"SUPPORTED\" per test with no\n","    correction. Benjamini-Hochberg FDR is now applied across the confirmatory\n","    family, and per-test two-sided bootstrap p-values are reported.\n"," 7. ISOTONIC CALIBRATION fit strictly on the inner-stopping slice; raw and\n","    calibrated probabilities both exported. The Bayes cost rule\n","    p* = (C_rev+C_fric)/(Amt+C_fric) is only meaningful on calibrated scores.\n"," 8. RELATIONAL-FEATURE LEAKAGE AUDIT. Explicit assertions that every history\n","    feature is strictly backward-looking (first occurrence of each entity must\n","    have seen_before == 0 and dt_diff == -1), plus a chronological-sort guard.\n","    v1 asserted none of this and relied on the reader trusting `cumcount()`.\n"," 9. ENTITY-OVERLAP AUDIT per fold (card/device seen-rate train->val). Without\n","    it, a first-seen vs. seen-before AP gap cannot be interpreted.\n","10. FEATURE-IMPORTANCE STABILITY across folds (Spearman rank correlation of\n","    gain), exported — evidence the relational features carry transferable\n","    structure rather than fold-specific noise.\n","11. `Recall@0.1%FPR` promoted into the printed report. It was computed but never\n","    displayed in v1, despite being the headline operating point for this work.\n","12. BUG FIX: v1's Stage-1 AP log line used doubled braces, printing the literal\n","    dict-comprehension source text instead of the values.\n","13. STAGE-1 ARTIFACT LOADER is schema-tolerant: accepts Stage 1 v2 columns\n","    (`stage1_prob_raw` / `stage1_prob_calibrated` / `stage1_prob_filled`) and\n","    falls back to the legacy `stage1_oof_prob`. In the v1 run BOTH Stage-1\n","    artifacts failed to resolve and H1/H1a/H1b were silently skipped — the\n","    central thesis hypothesis was never actually tested. Missing artifacts now\n","    raise a loud, explicit banner.\n","14. Determinism flags and explicit sub-seeds, matching Stage 1 v2.\n","\n","Retained protocol invariants\n","----------------------------\n","  - Equal-row deterministic chronological blocks; 1-4 dev, 5 sealed OOT.\n","  - 1-day boundary embargo on all REPORTED validation metrics.\n","  - Inner-split (last 20% by time) early stopping; never the reported block.\n","  - Reference rungs and paired bootstrap CIs on AP deltas.\n","  - Shuffled-entity null control (N1) isolating topology from feature count.\n","\"\"\"\n","\n","from __future__ import annotations\n","\n","import gc\n","import hashlib\n","import json\n","import os\n","import platform\n","import warnings\n","from datetime import datetime, timezone\n","\n","import lightgbm as lgb\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import sklearn\n","from sklearn.isotonic import IsotonicRegression\n","from sklearn.metrics import average_precision_score, roc_auc_score\n","\n","warnings.simplefilter(\"default\")\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=UserWarning, module=\"lightgbm\")\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\n","    \"ignore\",\n","    category=DeprecationWarning,\n","    message=r\"datetime\\.datetime\\.utcnow\\(\\) is deprecated.*\",\n",")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"229dfd2d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.678788Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.678129Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.683409Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.682386Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.013672,"end_time":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.685551+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.671879+00:00","status":"completed"},"provenance_fingerprint":true,"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# Dedicated fingerprint cell excluded from the canonical code-source snapshot.\n","NOTEBOOK_CODE_SHA256 = 'a2ef95b875f36194469341a03ce1b6af4d391a2ac36a25b6b080a1b2c148c78c'\n","NOTEBOOK_CODE_HASH_SCOPE = \"SHA-256 of UTF-8 json.dumps(code_sources, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(',', ':')); code_sources is the ordered list of joined code-cell sources, excluding cells with metadata.provenance_fingerprint == true. Excludes markdown, outputs and all metadata. Embedded build-time snapshot independently validated before publication; recompute after code edits.\"\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"44089e6a","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.697923Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.697546Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.709814Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.708821Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.021288,"end_time":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.711901+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.690613+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 1. Configuration\n","# ==============================================================================\n","CONFIG = {\n","    # --- Reproducibility & Schema ---\n","    \"SEED\": 42,\n","    \"TIME_COLUMN\": \"TransactionDT\",\n","    \"TARGET_COLUMN\": \"isFraud\",\n","    \"ID_COLUMN\": \"TransactionID\",\n","    \"AMOUNT_COLUMN\": \"TransactionAmt\",\n","\n","    # --- Temporal Split & Embargo Protocol ---\n","    \"N_BLOCKS\": 5,\n","    \"DEV_BLOCKS\": [1, 2, 3, 4],\n","    \"OOT_BLOCK\": 5,\n","    \"SECONDS_PER_DAY\": 86_400,\n","    \"EMBARGO_SECONDS\": 86_400,\n","\n","    # EMBARGO SEMANTICS — identical to Stage 1 v2.\n","    # The embargo de-biases *reported* metrics. It is NOT the causality device;\n","    # causality is guaranteed by train_max_dt <= score_min_dt assertions. The\n","    # feature-generation pass therefore runs embargo-off for full coverage.\n","    \"EMBARGO_IN_FEATURE_PASS\": False,\n","\n","    # --- Early Stopping & Validation Integrity ---\n","    \"INNER_VAL_FRAC\": 0.20,\n","    \"MIN_STOP_ROWS\": 5_000,\n","    \"MIN_STOP_POSITIVES\": 50,\n","\n","    # --- Block 1 OOF sub-fold scheme ---\n","    \"B1_SUBFOLDS\": 4,\n","\n","    # --- Boosting-round rule where early stopping is not viable ---\n","    \"FINAL_ROUNDS_RULE\": \"median\",       # {\"median\", \"last\", \"mean\"}\n","\n","    # --- Calibration ---\n","    \"CALIBRATION\": \"isotonic\",           # {\"isotonic\", \"none\"}\n","    \"EXPORT_CALIBRATED_OOF\": True,\n","\n","    # --- Cost Model (Bayes-Optimal Decision Boundary) ---\n","    \"C_REVIEW\": 10.0,\n","    \"C_FRICTION\": 25.0,\n","\n","    # --- Operational Triage & Bootstrap ---\n","    \"INVESTIGATION_CAPACITY\": 0.01,\n","    \"N_BOOTSTRAP\": 400,\n","    \"BOOTSTRAP_ALPHA\": 0.05,\n","    \"ACCEPTANCE_DELTA\": 0.005,\n","    \"FDR_ALPHA\": 0.05,                   # Benjamini-Hochberg level\n","\n","    # --- Experimental arms ---\n","    \"RUN_BASE_ONLY\": True,               # Internal H1 control (NEW, important)\n","    \"RUN_SHUFFLE_CONTROL\": True,         # N1 null: entity topology destroyed\n","    \"RUN_RELATIONAL_ONLY\": True,         # Standalone relational signal\n","\n","    # --- LightGBM Hyperparameters ---\n","    \"LGB_PARAMS\": {\n","        \"objective\": \"binary\",\n","        \"metric\": \"average_precision\",\n","        \"boosting_type\": \"gbdt\",\n","        \"learning_rate\": 0.03,\n","        \"num_leaves\": 256,\n","        \"max_depth\": -1,\n","        \"min_child_samples\": 50,\n","        # FIX: bagging_fraction is inert unless bagging_freq > 0.\n","        \"bagging_fraction\": 0.8,\n","        \"bagging_freq\": 1,\n","        \"feature_fraction\": 0.7,\n","        \"seed\": 42,\n","        \"bagging_seed\": 42,\n","        \"feature_fraction_seed\": 42,\n","        \"data_random_seed\": 42,\n","        \"deterministic\": True,\n","        \"force_row_wise\": True,\n","        \"n_jobs\": -1,\n","        \"verbose\": -1,\n","    },\n","    \"NUM_BOOST_ROUND\": 2000,\n","    \"EARLY_STOPPING_ROUNDS\": 50,\n","\n","    # --- Search Paths ---\n","    \"CANDIDATE_DATA_DIRS\": [\n","        \"/kaggle/input/competitions/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","        \"./data/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","        \"./data\",\n","        \".\",\n","    ],\n","    \"CANDIDATE_DECISION_PATHS\": [\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/ieee-cis-eda-leakage-audit/artifacts/feature_risk_table.csv\",\n","        \"./artifacts/feature_risk_table.csv\",\n","        \"./artifacts/feature_decisions.csv\",\n","        \"feature_risk_table.csv\",\n","        \"feature_decisions.csv\",\n","    ],\n","    \"CANDIDATE_STAGE1_RESULTS\": [\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/fork-of-stage-1-standalone-tabular-lightgbm-basel/artifacts/stage1_fold_results.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/stage-1-standalone-tabular-lightgbm-baseline/artifacts/stage1_fold_results.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/stage-1-standalone-tabular-lightgbm-baseline/stage1_fold_results.csv\",\n","        \"./artifacts/stage1_fold_results.csv\",\n","        \"stage1_fold_results.csv\",\n","    ],\n","    \"CANDIDATE_STAGE1_OOF\": [\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/fork-of-stage-1-standalone-tabular-lightgbm-basel/artifacts/stage1_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/stage-1-standalone-tabular-lightgbm-baseline/artifacts/stage1_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/stage-1-standalone-tabular-lightgbm-baseline/stage1_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"./artifacts/stage1_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","        \"stage1_oof_predictions.csv\",\n","    ],\n","    \"OUTPUT_DIR\": \"./artifacts\",\n","}\n","\n","TARGET_LEAKAGE_COLUMNS = [\n","    \"isFraud\",\n","    \"TransactionID\",\n","    \"TransactionDT\",\n","    \"elapsed_days\",\n","    \"day_index\",\n","    \"chrono_block\",\n","]\n","AUDIT_ONLY_COLUMNS = [\n","    \"uid_card\", \"uid_device\", \"card_first_seen\", \"device_first_seen\",\n","    \"stage1_prob_raw\", \"stage1_prob_calibrated\", \"stage1_prob_filled\",\n","    \"stage1_available\", \"stage1_missing\", \"stage1_source\", \"stage1_oof_prob\",\n","]\n","\n","np.random.seed(CONFIG[\"SEED\"])\n","os.makedirs(CONFIG[\"OUTPUT_DIR\"], exist_ok=True)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"79aa4c61","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.723956Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.723599Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.783629Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.782687Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.069278,"end_time":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.78588+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.716602+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 2. Shared Utilities (protocol-identical to Stage 1 v2)\n","# ==============================================================================\n","def file_sha256(path: str) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"SHA-256 of actual file bytes, streamed in bounded chunks.\"\"\"\n","    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n","    with open(path, \"rb\") as source:\n","        for chunk in iter(lambda: source.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n","            digest.update(chunk)\n","    return digest.hexdigest()\n","\n","\n","input_provenance: dict[str, dict] = {}\n","\n","\n","def record_input(name: str, path: str | None, status: str) -> None:\n","    \"\"\"Snapshot provenance at ingestion, including unavailable/rejected inputs.\"\"\"\n","    input_provenance[name] = {\n","        \"path\": os.path.realpath(path) if path is not None else None,\n","        \"status\": status,\n","        \"sha256\": file_sha256(path) if status == \"read\" else None,\n","    }\n","\n","\n","def resolve_path(candidates: list[str], target_file: str | None = None) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"Resolve the first existing directory (or dir/target_file) from candidates.\"\"\"\n","    for path in candidates:\n","        check_path = os.path.join(path, target_file) if target_file else path\n","        if os.path.exists(check_path):\n","            return check_path if target_file else path\n","    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Target {target_file or 'directory'} not found in {candidates}.\")\n","\n","\n","def resolve_first_existing(candidates: list[str]) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"Return the first candidate file path that exists.\"\"\"\n","    for path in candidates:\n","        if os.path.exists(path):\n","            return path\n","    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"None of these paths exist: {candidates}\")\n","\n","\n","def reduce_memory(frame: pd.DataFrame, label: str = \"\") -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Downcast numeric columns to shrink the working set without value loss.\"\"\"\n","    before = frame.memory_usage(deep=False).sum() / 1024 ** 2\n","    for col in frame.columns:\n","        kind = frame[col].dtype.kind\n","        if kind == \"i\":\n","            frame[col] = pd.to_numeric(frame[col], downcast=\"integer\")\n","        elif kind == \"f\":\n","            frame[col] = frame[col].astype(np.float32)\n","    after = frame.memory_usage(deep=False).sum() / 1024 ** 2\n","    saved = (before - after) / max(before, 1e-9)\n","    print(f\"    Memory downcast{(' [' + label + ']') if label else ''}: \"\n","          f\"{before:.1f} MB -> {after:.1f} MB ({saved:.1%} saved)\")\n","    return frame\n","\n","\n","def create_temporal_blocks(frame: pd.DataFrame, n_blocks: int,\n","                           time_col: str = \"TransactionDT\",\n","                           id_col: str = \"TransactionID\") -> pd.Series:\n","    \"\"\"Assign equal-row-count chronological block labels 1..n_blocks deterministically.\"\"\"\n","    order = frame.sort_values([time_col, id_col], kind=\"mergesort\").index\n","    position = pd.Series(np.arange(len(order)), index=order)\n","    labels = np.minimum((position.values * n_blocks) // len(order), n_blocks - 1) + 1\n","    return pd.Series(labels.astype(np.int16), index=order).reindex(frame.index)\n","\n","\n","def alert_threshold(amounts: np.ndarray,\n","                    c_rev: float = CONFIG[\"C_REVIEW\"],\n","                    c_fric: float = CONFIG[\"C_FRICTION\"]) -> np.ndarray:\n","    \"\"\"Bayes-optimal per-transaction alert threshold p* = (C_rev+C_fric)/(Amt+C_fric).\"\"\"\n","    amounts_arr = np.asarray(amounts, dtype=float)\n","    return np.minimum((c_rev + c_fric) / (amounts_arr + c_fric), 1.0)\n","\n","\n","def expected_calibration_error(y_true: np.ndarray, y_prob: np.ndarray,\n","                               n_bins: int = 20, strategy: str = \"uniform\") -> float:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Bin-weighted ECE. Report BOTH strategies.\n","\n","    'uniform'  : equal-width bins. At ~3.5% prevalence the [0,0.05) bin holds\n","                 ~95% of the mass, so this statistic flatters every model.\n","    'quantile' : equal-frequency bins — far more discriminating in the\n","                 operationally relevant high-score region.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    y_true_arr = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=float)\n","    y_prob_arr = np.clip(np.asarray(y_prob, dtype=float), 0.0, 1.0)\n","    n = len(y_true_arr)\n","    if n == 0:\n","        return float(\"nan\")\n","\n","    if strategy == \"quantile\":\n","        edges = np.unique(np.quantile(y_prob_arr, np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1)))\n","        if len(edges) < 3:\n","            return expected_calibration_error(y_true_arr, y_prob_arr, n_bins, \"uniform\")\n","        bin_idx = np.clip(np.digitize(y_prob_arr, edges[1:-1], right=False), 0, len(edges) - 2)\n","        n_eff = len(edges) - 1\n","    else:\n","        edges = np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1)\n","        bin_idx = np.clip(np.digitize(y_prob_arr, edges[1:-1], right=False), 0, n_bins - 1)\n","        n_eff = n_bins\n","\n","    total_error = 0.0\n","    for b in range(n_eff):\n","        mask = bin_idx == b\n","        count = int(mask.sum())\n","        if count > 0:\n","            total_error += count * abs(y_prob_arr[mask].mean() - y_true_arr[mask].mean())\n","    return float(total_error / n)\n","\n","\n","def compute_metrics(y_true: np.ndarray, y_prob: np.ndarray, amounts: np.ndarray,\n","                    capacity: float = CONFIG[\"INVESTIGATION_CAPACITY\"]) -> dict[str, float]:\n","    \"\"\"Ranking, calibration, triage and economic metrics for one scored window.\"\"\"\n","    y_true = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=int)\n","    y_prob = np.asarray(y_prob, dtype=float)\n","    amounts = np.asarray(amounts, dtype=float)\n","\n","    ap = float(average_precision_score(y_true, y_prob))\n","    try:\n","        roc = float(roc_auc_score(y_true, y_prob))\n","    except ValueError:\n","        roc = float(\"nan\")\n","\n","    p_safe = np.clip(y_prob, 1e-15, 1.0 - 1e-15)\n","    log_loss = float(-np.mean(y_true * np.log(p_safe) + (1 - y_true) * np.log(1.0 - p_safe)))\n","    brier = float(np.mean((y_prob - y_true) ** 2))\n","    ece_u = expected_calibration_error(y_true, y_prob, 20, \"uniform\")\n","    ece_q = expected_calibration_error(y_true, y_prob, 20, \"quantile\")\n","\n","    order = np.lexsort((-amounts, -y_prob))\n","    y_sorted = y_true[order]\n","    n_neg = int((y_sorted == 0).sum())\n","    n_pos = int((y_sorted == 1).sum())\n","    cum_fp = (y_sorted == 0).cumsum()\n","\n","    def recall_at_fpr(target_fpr: float) -> float:\n","        budget = int(np.floor(target_fpr * n_neg))\n","        alerted_pos = int(y_sorted[cum_fp <= budget].sum())\n","        return float(alerted_pos / n_pos) if n_pos > 0 else 0.0\n","\n","    k_cap = max(1, int(np.floor(capacity * len(y_sorted))))\n","    prec_at_cap = float(y_sorted[:k_cap].mean())\n","    rec_at_cap = float(y_sorted[:k_cap].sum() / n_pos) if n_pos > 0 else 0.0\n","\n","    def financial_loss(predictions: np.ndarray) -> float:\n","        fn_mask = (y_true == 1) & (predictions == 0)\n","        fp_mask = (y_true == 0) & (predictions == 1)\n","        return float(amounts[fn_mask].sum()\n","                     + predictions.sum() * CONFIG[\"C_REVIEW\"]\n","                     + fp_mask.sum() * CONFIG[\"C_FRICTION\"])\n","\n","    preds_cost_rule = (y_prob > alert_threshold(amounts)).astype(int)\n","    preds_flat_half = (y_prob >= 0.5).astype(int)\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"AP\": ap,\n","        \"ROC_AUC\": roc,\n","        \"LogLoss\": log_loss,\n","        \"Brier\": brier,\n","        \"ECE\": ece_u,\n","        \"ECE_quantile\": ece_q,\n","        \"Recall@0.1%FPR\": recall_at_fpr(0.001),\n","        \"Recall@1.0%FPR\": recall_at_fpr(0.010),\n","        f\"Prec@{capacity:.1%}cap\": prec_at_cap,\n","        f\"Recall@{capacity:.1%}cap\": rec_at_cap,\n","        \"Loss_cost_rule\": financial_loss(preds_cost_rule),\n","        \"Loss_flat_0.5\": financial_loss(preds_flat_half),\n","        \"Loss_no_model\": float(amounts[y_true == 1].sum()),\n","        \"AlertRate\": float(preds_cost_rule.mean()),\n","    }\n","\n","\n","def bootstrap_ap_delta(y_true: np.ndarray, p_new: np.ndarray, p_ref: np.ndarray,\n","                       n_boot: int = CONFIG[\"N_BOOTSTRAP\"],\n","                       alpha: float = CONFIG[\"BOOTSTRAP_ALPHA\"],\n","                       seed: int = CONFIG[\"SEED\"]) -> dict[str, float | int]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Paired bootstrap of AP(p_new) - AP(p_ref) over identical resampled rows.\n","\n","    Returns a two-sided bootstrap p-value in addition to the CI, so the family\n","    of confirmatory tests can be FDR-corrected downstream.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    y_arr = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=int)\n","    p_new_arr = np.asarray(p_new, dtype=float)\n","    p_ref_arr = np.asarray(p_ref, dtype=float)\n","    n = len(y_arr)\n","\n","    observed = float(average_precision_score(y_arr, p_new_arr)\n","                     - average_precision_score(y_arr, p_ref_arr))\n","    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n","    deltas = np.empty(n_boot, dtype=float)\n","    valid = 0\n","    for _ in range(n_boot):\n","        idx = rng.integers(0, n, size=n)\n","        y_b = y_arr[idx]\n","        if y_b.sum() == 0 or y_b.sum() == n:\n","            continue\n","        deltas[valid] = (average_precision_score(y_b, p_new_arr[idx])\n","                         - average_precision_score(y_b, p_ref_arr[idx]))\n","        valid += 1\n","\n","    deltas = deltas[:valid]\n","    if valid == 0:\n","        return {\"delta\": observed, \"ci_low\": np.nan, \"ci_high\": np.nan,\n","                \"p_win\": np.nan, \"p_value\": np.nan, \"n_boot\": 0}\n","\n","    ci_low, ci_high = np.percentile(deltas, [100 * alpha / 2, 100 * (1.0 - alpha / 2)])\n","    p_win = float((deltas > 0.0).mean())\n","    # Two-sided bootstrap p-value, floored at 1/valid (resolution limit).\n","    p_two = 2.0 * min(p_win, 1.0 - p_win)\n","    p_two = float(min(1.0, max(p_two, 1.0 / valid)))\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"delta\": observed,\n","        \"ci_low\": float(ci_low),\n","        \"ci_high\": float(ci_high),\n","        \"p_win\": p_win,\n","        \"p_value\": p_two,\n","        \"n_boot\": int(valid),\n","    }\n","\n","\n","def benjamini_hochberg(p_values: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Benjamini-Hochberg FDR control.\n","\n","    Returns (reject_flags, adjusted_p_values). Necessary here because the\n","    confirmatory family spans several hypotheses x several scopes over largely\n","    overlapping rows; declaring each \"SUPPORTED\" independently inflates the\n","    family-wise error rate.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    p = np.asarray(p_values, dtype=float)\n","    m = len(p)\n","    if m == 0:\n","        return np.array([], dtype=bool), np.array([], dtype=float)\n","\n","    order = np.argsort(p)\n","    ranked = p[order]\n","    adj_sorted = np.minimum.accumulate((ranked * m / np.arange(1, m + 1))[::-1])[::-1]\n","    adj_sorted = np.clip(adj_sorted, 0.0, 1.0)\n","\n","    adjusted = np.empty(m, dtype=float)\n","    adjusted[order] = adj_sorted\n","    return adjusted <= alpha, adjusted\n","\n","\n","def build_entity_uids(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> tuple[pd.Series, pd.Series]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Registration-anchored entity proxies.\n","\n","    Anchor = day_index - D1 (approximate account-open date). These UID strings\n","    are audit/aggregation keys only and are never passed to the model as\n","    features — that would be high-cardinality target-adjacent memorisation.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    anchor = np.where(\n","        frame[\"D1\"].isna(),\n","        \"na\",\n","        (frame[\"day_index\"] - frame[\"D1\"].fillna(0)).astype(\"int64\").astype(str),\n","    )\n","\n","    def col_str(name: str, fill) -> pd.Series:\n","        if name not in frame.columns:\n","            return pd.Series([\"na\"] * len(frame), index=frame.index)\n","        return frame[name].fillna(fill).astype(str)\n","\n","    uid_card = (\n","        col_str(\"card1\", -1) + \"_\" + col_str(\"card2\", -1) + \"_\"\n","        + col_str(\"card3\", -1) + \"_\" + col_str(\"card4\", \"na\") + \"_\"\n","        + col_str(\"card5\", -1) + \"_\" + col_str(\"card6\", \"na\") + \"_\"\n","        + col_str(\"addr1\", -1) + \"_\" + pd.Series(anchor, index=frame.index)\n","    )\n","    uid_device = (\n","        col_str(\"DeviceInfo\", \"no_dev\") + \"_\"\n","        + col_str(\"id_30\", \"no_os\") + \"_\"\n","        + col_str(\"id_31\", \"no_brw\")\n","    )\n","    return uid_card, uid_device\n","\n","\n","def first_seen_flag(entity_series: pd.Series) -> np.ndarray:\n","    \"\"\"True on an entity's first chronological appearance (depends only on the past).\"\"\"\n","    return ~entity_series.duplicated(keep=\"first\").to_numpy()\n","\n","\n","def entity_overlap_rate(frame: pd.DataFrame, train_idx, score_idx, col: str) -> float:\n","    \"\"\"Share of scored rows whose entity was already observed in the training window.\"\"\"\n","    seen = set(frame.loc[train_idx, col].unique())\n","    return float(frame.loc[score_idx, col].isin(seen).mean())\n","\n","\n","def assert_causal(frame: pd.DataFrame, train_idx, score_idx, label: str,\n","                  time_col: str = CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]) -> None:\n","    \"\"\"Hard guarantee that every training row precedes (or ties) every scored row.\"\"\"\n","    if len(train_idx) == 0 or len(score_idx) == 0:\n","        return\n","    train_max = frame.loc[train_idx, time_col].max()\n","    score_min = frame.loc[score_idx, time_col].min()\n","    assert train_max <= score_min, (\n","        f\"CAUSALITY VIOLATION [{label}]: train_max_dt={train_max} > score_min_dt={score_min}\"\n","    )\n","\n","\n","def time_ordered_inner_split(frame: pd.DataFrame, train_idx, frac: float,\n","                             time_col: str = CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]):\n","    \"\"\"Split a training index into (fit, stop) where stop is the latest `frac` by time.\"\"\"\n","    train_dt = frame.loc[train_idx, time_col].to_numpy()\n","    threshold = np.quantile(train_dt, 1.0 - frac)\n","    return train_idx[train_dt < threshold], train_idx[train_dt >= threshold]\n","\n","\n","def train_causal_model(frame: pd.DataFrame, train_idx, features: list[str],\n","                       label: str, fallback_rounds: int):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Fit LightGBM on `train_idx`, early-stopping on a time-ordered inner split.\n","\n","    Returns (model, best_iter, fit_idx, stop_idx, used_early_stopping). Falls back\n","    to a fixed round count when the stopping slice is too thin to be trustworthy,\n","    rather than early-stopping on noise.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    target = CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"]\n","    fit_idx, stop_idx = time_ordered_inner_split(frame, train_idx, CONFIG[\"INNER_VAL_FRAC\"])\n","    n_stop_pos = int(frame.loc[stop_idx, target].sum()) if len(stop_idx) else 0\n","    viable = (len(stop_idx) >= CONFIG[\"MIN_STOP_ROWS\"]\n","              and n_stop_pos >= CONFIG[\"MIN_STOP_POSITIVES\"])\n","\n","    if viable:\n","        fit_data = lgb.Dataset(frame.loc[fit_idx, features],\n","                               label=frame.loc[fit_idx, target].values)\n","        stop_data = lgb.Dataset(frame.loc[stop_idx, features],\n","                                label=frame.loc[stop_idx, target].values,\n","                                reference=fit_data)\n","        model = lgb.train(\n","            CONFIG[\"LGB_PARAMS\"], fit_data,\n","            num_boost_round=CONFIG[\"NUM_BOOST_ROUND\"],\n","            valid_sets=[stop_data],\n","            callbacks=[lgb.early_stopping(CONFIG[\"EARLY_STOPPING_ROUNDS\"], verbose=False)],\n","        )\n","        return model, int(model.best_iteration), fit_idx, stop_idx, True\n","\n","    warnings.warn(\n","        f\"[{label}] inner stopping set too small (rows={len(stop_idx)}, \"\n","        f\"pos={n_stop_pos}); using fixed {fallback_rounds} rounds.\",\n","        RuntimeWarning,\n","    )\n","    fit_data = lgb.Dataset(frame.loc[train_idx, features],\n","                           label=frame.loc[train_idx, target].values)\n","    model = lgb.train(CONFIG[\"LGB_PARAMS\"], fit_data, num_boost_round=fallback_rounds)\n","    return model, int(fallback_rounds), train_idx, np.array([], dtype=int), False\n","\n","\n","def fit_calibrator(model, frame: pd.DataFrame, stop_idx, features: list[str], best_iter: int):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Isotonic calibration fit ONLY on the inner-stopping slice.\n","\n","    That slice is already spent for reporting purposes, so it is the only honest\n","    calibration surface that does not touch the validation block.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if CONFIG[\"CALIBRATION\"] != \"isotonic\" or len(stop_idx) == 0:\n","        return None\n","    y_stop = frame.loc[stop_idx, CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"]].values\n","    if y_stop.sum() < CONFIG[\"MIN_STOP_POSITIVES\"]:\n","        return None\n","    p_stop = model.predict(frame.loc[stop_idx, features], num_iteration=best_iter)\n","    iso = IsotonicRegression(y_min=0.0, y_max=1.0, out_of_bounds=\"clip\")\n","    iso.fit(p_stop, y_stop)\n","    return iso\n","\n","\n","def apply_calibrator(calibrator, probs: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n","    \"\"\"Apply a fitted calibrator; identity passthrough when absent.\"\"\"\n","    if calibrator is None:\n","        return probs\n","    return np.clip(calibrator.predict(probs), 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n","\n","\n","def rounds_from_history(history: dict[int, int], rule: str, floor: int = 10) -> int:\n","    \"\"\"Derive a boosting-round schedule for models that cannot early-stop.\"\"\"\n","    values = list(history.values())\n","    if not values:\n","        return max(floor, 100)\n","    if rule == \"last\":\n","        chosen = values[-1]\n","    elif rule == \"mean\":\n","        chosen = float(np.mean(values))\n","    else:\n","        chosen = float(np.median(values))\n","    return max(floor, int(round(chosen)))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"511bc1cb","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.798235Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.797811Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T09:12:17.992496Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T09:12:17.991437Z"},"papermill":{"duration":39.20354,"end_time":"2026-09-30T09:12:17.99469+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T09:11:38.79115+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[1] Resolving environment and loading raw data...\n","    Selected data directory: /kaggle/input/competitions/ieee-fraud-detection\n","    Joining train_identity.csv via left join...\n","    Memory downcast [raw]: 1955.4 MB -> 1044.7 MB (46.6% saved)\n","[2] Enforcing deterministic chronological sort and block construction...\n","    Block 5 OOT quarantine: PASSED (sealed; scored later, never trained on).\n","    Block profile (prevalence drift check):\n","                rows  fraud_rate  first_day  last_day\n","chrono_block                                         \n","1             118108    0.023927          0        25\n","2             118108    0.040065         25        63\n","3             118108    0.037508         63       100\n","4             118108    0.039041        100       140\n","5             118108    0.034409        140       181\n"]}],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 3. Data Loading, Temporal Structuring, OOT Quarantine\n","# ==============================================================================\n","print(\"[1] Resolving environment and loading raw data...\")\n","data_dir = resolve_path(CONFIG[\"CANDIDATE_DATA_DIRS\"])\n","print(f\"    Selected data directory: {data_dir}\")\n","\n","trans_df = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(data_dir, \"train_transaction.csv\"))\n","record_input(\"train_transaction\", os.path.join(data_dir, \"train_transaction.csv\"), \"read\")\n","id_path = os.path.join(data_dir, \"train_identity.csv\")\n","\n","if os.path.exists(id_path):\n","    print(\"    Joining train_identity.csv via left join...\")\n","    id_df = pd.read_csv(id_path)\n","    record_input(\"train_identity\", id_path, \"read\")\n","    df = trans_df.merge(id_df, on=CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"], how=\"left\")\n","    del id_df\n","else:\n","    record_input(\"train_identity\", id_path, \"missing\")\n","    print(\"    WARNING: train_identity.csv not found. Transaction columns only.\")\n","    df = trans_df.copy()\n","\n","del trans_df\n","gc.collect()\n","\n","assert df[CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"]].is_unique, \"Fatal: duplicate TransactionIDs post-merge.\"\n","assert df[CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]].notna().all(), \"Fatal: null TransactionDT.\"\n","assert df[CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"]].notna().all(), \"Fatal: null isFraud.\"\n","assert set(df[CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"]].unique()) <= {0, 1}, \"Fatal: target not binary.\"\n","\n","df = reduce_memory(df, \"raw\")\n","\n","print(\"[2] Enforcing deterministic chronological sort and block construction...\")\n","df = df.sort_values([CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"], CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"]],\n","                    kind=\"mergesort\").reset_index(drop=True)\n","\n","# Relational features below rely on this ordering. Assert it rather than assume it.\n","assert df[CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]].is_monotonic_increasing, (\n","    \"Fatal: frame is not chronologically sorted; every expanding-history feature \"\n","    \"would silently become non-causal.\"\n",")\n","\n","t0 = int(df[CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]].min())\n","df[\"elapsed_days\"] = ((df[CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]] - t0) / CONFIG[\"SECONDS_PER_DAY\"]).astype(np.float32)\n","df[\"day_index\"] = ((df[CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]] - t0) // CONFIG[\"SECONDS_PER_DAY\"]).astype(np.int16)\n","df[\"chrono_block\"] = create_temporal_blocks(df, n_blocks=CONFIG[\"N_BLOCKS\"])\n","\n","df[\"uid_card\"], df[\"uid_device\"] = build_entity_uids(df)\n","df[\"card_first_seen\"] = first_seen_flag(df[\"uid_card\"])\n","df[\"device_first_seen\"] = first_seen_flag(df[\"uid_device\"])\n","\n","dev_mask = (df[\"chrono_block\"] < CONFIG[\"OOT_BLOCK\"]).to_numpy()\n","oot_mask = (df[\"chrono_block\"] == CONFIG[\"OOT_BLOCK\"]).to_numpy()\n","assert df.loc[dev_mask, CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]].max() <= df.loc[oot_mask, CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]].min(), (\n","    \"Fatal: OOT Block 5 overlaps development Blocks 1-4.\"\n",")\n","assert not (set(df.loc[dev_mask, CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"]]) & set(df.loc[oot_mask, CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"]])), (\n","    \"Fatal: row-ID collision between development and OOT sets.\"\n",")\n","OOT_INDEX = set(df.index[oot_mask].tolist())\n","print(\"    Block 5 OOT quarantine: PASSED (sealed; scored later, never trained on).\")\n","\n","block_profile = (\n","    df.groupby(\"chrono_block\")\n","      .agg(rows=(CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"], \"size\"),\n","           fraud_rate=(CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"], \"mean\"),\n","           first_day=(\"day_index\", \"min\"),\n","           last_day=(\"day_index\", \"max\"))\n",")\n","print(\"    Block profile (prevalence drift check):\")\n","print(block_profile.to_string())"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"id":"77b17d54","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T09:12:18.007287Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T09:12:18.006878Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T09:12:20.455581Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T09:12:20.454439Z"},"papermill":{"duration":2.458111,"end_time":"2026-09-30T09:12:20.457766+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T09:12:17.999655+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[3] Ingesting feature-decision ledger and Stage 1 artifacts...\n","    Loaded decisions ledger: /kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/ieee-cis-eda-leakage-audit/artifacts/feature_risk_table.csv\n","    Retained 371 base features from audit screening.\n","    Loaded Stage 1 reference APs: {1: 0.5254, 2: 0.4812, 3: 0.533}\n","    Merged Stage 1 OOF from 'stage1_prob_raw' | dev coverage 93.8% | OOT coverage 100.0%\n"]}],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 4. Feature Ledger & Stage 1 Artifact Ingestion\n","# ==============================================================================\n","print(\"[3] Ingesting feature-decision ledger and Stage 1 artifacts...\")\n","decision_file = resolve_first_existing(CONFIG[\"CANDIDATE_DECISION_PATHS\"])\n","print(f\"    Loaded decisions ledger: {decision_file}\")\n","decisions_df = pd.read_csv(decision_file)\n","record_input(\"decision_ledger\", decision_file, \"read\")\n","\n","action_col = \"action\" if \"action\" in decisions_df.columns else \"verdict\"\n","drop_filter = decisions_df[action_col].astype(str).str.lower().str.startswith(\"drop\")\n","accepted_features = decisions_df.loc[~drop_filter, \"feature\"].tolist()\n","\n","base_features = [\n","    col for col in accepted_features\n","    if col in df.columns\n","    and col not in TARGET_LEAKAGE_COLUMNS\n","    and col not in AUDIT_ONLY_COLUMNS\n","]\n","assert base_features, \"Fatal: no base features survived the audit filter.\"\n","print(f\"    Retained {len(base_features)} base features from audit screening.\")\n","\n","# --- Stage 1 fold results (secondary, cross-run reference only) ---\n","STAGE1_AP: dict = {}\n","stage1_results_path = None\n","record_input(\"stage1_results\", None, \"unavailable\")\n","try:\n","    stage1_results_path = resolve_first_existing(CONFIG[\"CANDIDATE_STAGE1_RESULTS\"])\n","    stage1_df = pd.read_csv(stage1_results_path).set_index(\"fold\")\n","    record_input(\"stage1_results\", stage1_results_path, \"read\")\n","    STAGE1_AP = {int(k): float(v) for k, v in stage1_df[\"AP\"].to_dict().items()}\n","    # BUG FIX: v1 double-braced this f-string and printed the literal source text.\n","    pretty = {k: round(v, 4) for k, v in STAGE1_AP.items()}\n","    print(f\"    Loaded Stage 1 reference APs: {pretty}\")\n","except FileNotFoundError:\n","    print(\"    [WARNING] Stage 1 fold results not found — cross-run AP reference unavailable.\")\n","\n","# --- Stage 1 per-row OOF scores (primary H1 comparator) ---\n","# Schema-tolerant: Stage 1 v2 emits stage1_prob_raw / _calibrated / _filled;\n","# Stage 1 v1 emitted stage1_oof_prob.\n","STAGE1_OOF_AVAILABLE = False\n","stage1_oof_path = None\n","record_input(\"stage1_oof\", None, \"unavailable\")\n","try:\n","    stage1_oof_path = resolve_first_existing(CONFIG[\"CANDIDATE_STAGE1_OOF\"])\n","    s1_oof = pd.read_csv(stage1_oof_path)\n","    record_input(\"stage1_oof\", stage1_oof_path, \"read\")\n","\n","    prob_col = next(\n","        (c for c in [\"stage1_prob_raw\", \"stage1_prob_calibrated\",\n","                     \"stage1_prob_filled\", \"stage1_oof_prob\"] if c in s1_oof.columns),\n","        None,\n","    )\n","    if prob_col is None:\n","        input_provenance[\"stage1_oof\"][\"status\"] = \"read_schema_rejected\"\n","        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"No recognised Stage-1 probability column in {stage1_oof_path}\")\n","\n","    keep = [CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"], prob_col]\n","    if \"stage1_source\" in s1_oof.columns:\n","        keep.append(\"stage1_source\")\n","    s1_oof = s1_oof[keep].rename(columns={prob_col: \"stage1_prob_raw\"})\n","\n","    df = df.merge(s1_oof, on=CONFIG[\"ID_COLUMN\"], how=\"left\")\n","    STAGE1_OOF_AVAILABLE = True\n","    cov_dev = df.loc[dev_mask, \"stage1_prob_raw\"].notna().mean()\n","    cov_oot = df.loc[oot_mask, \"stage1_prob_raw\"].notna().mean()\n","    print(f\"    Merged Stage 1 OOF from '{prob_col}' | dev coverage {cov_dev:.1%} \"\n","          f\"| OOT coverage {cov_oot:.1%}\")\n","    if cov_oot == 0:\n","        print(\"    [NOTE] Stage 1 artifact has no Block 5 coverage (legacy v1 output). \"\n","              \"Joint OOT evaluation will require re-running Stage 1 v2.\")\n","except FileNotFoundError as exc:\n","    df[\"stage1_prob_raw\"] = np.nan\n","    print(\"\\n\" + \"!\" * 78)\n","    print(\"[CRITICAL] Stage 1 OOF predictions NOT FOUND.\")\n","    print(f\"           {exc}\")\n","    print(\"           H1 / H1a / H1b (the central thesis hypotheses) CANNOT be\")\n","    print(\"           tested against Stage 1 and will be SKIPPED. The internal\")\n","    print(\"           `base_only` arm still provides a valid paired control.\")\n","    print(\"!\" * 78 + \"\\n\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":7,"id":"32acc705","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T09:12:20.469988Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T09:12:20.469659Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T09:12:26.774301Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T09:12:26.772695Z"},"papermill":{"duration":6.313776,"end_time":"2026-09-30T09:12:26.776657+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T09:12:20.462881+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[4] Engineering time-causal relational features (expanding history only)...\n","      causality audit [uid_card]: PASSED (37.7% first-seen, max history 1413)\n","      causality audit [uid_device]: PASSED (1.1% first-seen, max history 449950)\n","    Memory downcast [relational]: 42.8 MB -> 42.8 MB (0.0% saved)\n","    Added 19 relational features.\n","    Stage 2 feature space: 390 (371 base + 19 relational).\n","    Building shuffled-entity null control (entity topology destroyed, feature count preserved)...\n","    Memory downcast [relational_shuffled]: 42.8 MB -> 42.8 MB (0.0% saved)\n","    Control feature space: 390 columns (same cardinality as the real arm).\n","    Categorical features cast for LightGBM: 0\n"]}],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 5. Relational Feature Engineering (strictly backward-looking)\n","# ==============================================================================\n","print(\"[4] Engineering time-causal relational features (expanding history only)...\")\n","\n","\n","def build_relational_features(df_in: pd.DataFrame, card_col: str, device_col: str,\n","                              suffix: str = \"\") -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Entity-history statistics computed strictly over prior rows (t_hist < t).\n","\n","    The current row is excluded from every count, sum and mean. `cumcount()`\n","    yields the number of PRIOR occurrences; cumulative sums have the current\n","    value subtracted back out. Input must be chronologically sorted.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    out: dict[str, np.ndarray] = {}\n","    amt_curr = df_in[\"TransactionAmt\"].to_numpy(dtype=np.float32)\n","\n","    for name, col in [(\"card\", card_col), (\"device\", device_col)]:\n","        key = f\"uid_{name}{suffix}\"\n","        g = df_in.groupby(col, sort=False)\n","\n","        # 1. Count of prior appearances (0 on first sighting).\n","        seen_before = g.cumcount().to_numpy(dtype=np.float32)\n","        out[f\"{key}_seen_before\"] = seen_before\n","\n","        # 2. Inter-arrival gap in seconds; -1 sentinel on first sighting.\n","        prev_dt = g[\"TransactionDT\"].shift(1)\n","        out[f\"{key}_dt_diff\"] = (df_in[\"TransactionDT\"] - prev_dt).fillna(-1.0).to_numpy(dtype=np.float32)\n","\n","        # 3. Running monetary statistics over history only.\n","        running_sum = (g[\"TransactionAmt\"].cumsum() - df_in[\"TransactionAmt\"]).to_numpy(dtype=np.float32)\n","        with np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\", invalid=\"ignore\"):\n","            running_mean = np.where(seen_before > 0, running_sum / seen_before, amt_curr)\n","        running_mean = np.nan_to_num(running_mean, nan=amt_curr).astype(np.float32)\n","\n","        out[f\"{key}_amt_running_mean\"] = running_mean\n","        out[f\"{key}_amt_ratio\"] = (amt_curr / (running_mean + 1.0)).astype(np.float32)\n","        out[f\"{key}_amt_diff\"] = (amt_curr - running_mean).astype(np.float32)\n","\n","    # 4. Card-anchored C-series running means (history only).\n","    card_seen = out[f\"uid_card{suffix}_seen_before\"]\n","    for c_col in [\"C1\", \"C2\", \"C13\", \"C14\"]:\n","        if c_col in df_in.columns:\n","            c_sum = (df_in.groupby(card_col, sort=False)[c_col].cumsum()\n","                     - df_in[c_col]).to_numpy(dtype=np.float32)\n","            with np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\", invalid=\"ignore\"):\n","                c_mean = np.where(card_seen > 0, c_sum / card_seen, 0.0)\n","            out[f\"uid_card{suffix}_{c_col}_running_mean\"] = np.nan_to_num(c_mean, nan=0.0).astype(np.float32)\n","\n","    # 5. Expanding counts for categorical proxies (dropna=False preserves missingness signal).\n","    for cat in [\"card1\", \"card2\", \"addr1\", \"P_emaildomain\", \"R_emaildomain\"]:\n","        if cat in df_in.columns:\n","            out[f\"{cat}{suffix}_seen_before\"] = (\n","                df_in.groupby(cat, sort=False, dropna=False).cumcount().to_numpy(dtype=np.float32)\n","            )\n","\n","    return pd.DataFrame(out, index=df_in.index)\n","\n","\n","def audit_relational_causality(frame: pd.DataFrame, feat: pd.DataFrame,\n","                               uid_col: str, key: str) -> None:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Assert that history features are strictly backward-looking.\n","\n","    On an entity's FIRST appearance there is by construction no history, so\n","    seen_before must be exactly 0 and dt_diff must be the -1 sentinel. Any\n","    violation means future information has leaked backwards. v1 asserted none\n","    of this.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    first = first_seen_flag(frame[uid_col])\n","    sb = feat[f\"{key}_seen_before\"].to_numpy()\n","    dt = feat[f\"{key}_dt_diff\"].to_numpy()\n","\n","    assert np.all(sb[first] == 0), (\n","        f\"LEAKAGE [{key}]: first-seen rows carry non-zero history counts.\"\n","    )\n","    assert np.all(dt[first] == -1.0), (\n","        f\"LEAKAGE [{key}]: first-seen rows carry a finite inter-arrival gap.\"\n","    )\n","    assert np.all(sb >= 0), f\"LEAKAGE [{key}]: negative history count.\"\n","    print(f\"      causality audit [{key}]: PASSED \"\n","          f\"({first.mean():.1%} first-seen, max history {sb.max():.0f})\")\n","\n","\n","rel_features_df = build_relational_features(df, \"uid_card\", \"uid_device\")\n","audit_relational_causality(df, rel_features_df, \"uid_card\", \"uid_card\")\n","audit_relational_causality(df, rel_features_df, \"uid_device\", \"uid_device\")\n","rel_features_df = reduce_memory(rel_features_df, \"relational\")\n","\n","df = pd.concat([df, rel_features_df], axis=1)\n","relational_cols = list(rel_features_df.columns)\n","stage2_features = base_features + relational_cols\n","del rel_features_df\n","gc.collect()\n","\n","print(f\"    Added {len(relational_cols)} relational features.\")\n","print(f\"    Stage 2 feature space: {len(stage2_features)} \"\n","      f\"({len(base_features)} base + {len(relational_cols)} relational).\")\n","\n","# --- Shuffled-entity null control features (N1) ---\n","control_features: list[str] = []\n","if CONFIG[\"RUN_SHUFFLE_CONTROL\"]:\n","    print(\"    Building shuffled-entity null control (entity topology destroyed,\"\n","          \" feature count preserved)...\")\n","    rng = np.random.default_rng(CONFIG[\"SEED\"])\n","    shuffled_df = pd.DataFrame({\n","        \"TransactionDT\": df[\"TransactionDT\"],\n","        \"TransactionAmt\": df[\"TransactionAmt\"],\n","        \"uid_card_shuf\": rng.permutation(df[\"uid_card\"].values),\n","        \"uid_device_shuf\": rng.permutation(df[\"uid_device\"].values),\n","    }, index=df.index)\n","\n","    for c_col in [\"C1\", \"C2\", \"C13\", \"C14\"]:\n","        if c_col in df.columns:\n","            shuffled_df[c_col] = df[c_col]\n","    for col in [\"card1\", \"card2\", \"addr1\", \"P_emaildomain\", \"R_emaildomain\"]:\n","        if col in df.columns:\n","            shuffled_df[col] = rng.permutation(df[col].values)\n","\n","    rel_shuf_df = build_relational_features(\n","        shuffled_df, \"uid_card_shuf\", \"uid_device_shuf\", suffix=\"_shuf\"\n","    )\n","    rel_shuf_df = reduce_memory(rel_shuf_df, \"relational_shuffled\")\n","    df = pd.concat([df, rel_shuf_df], axis=1)\n","    control_features = base_features + list(rel_shuf_df.columns)\n","    del shuffled_df, rel_shuf_df\n","    gc.collect()\n","    print(f\"    Control feature space: {len(control_features)} columns \"\n","          \"(same cardinality as the real arm).\")\n","\n","# --- Categorical casting across every arm ---\n","all_model_cols = sorted(set(stage2_features) | set(control_features) | set(relational_cols))\n","cat_cols = [c for c in all_model_cols\n","            if df[c].dtype == \"object\" or str(df[c].dtype) == \"category\"]\n","for c in cat_cols:\n","    df[c] = df[c].astype(\"category\")\n","print(f\"    Categorical features cast for LightGBM: {len(cat_cols)}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":8,"id":"67561558","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T09:12:26.792297Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T09:12:26.79159Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T09:21:56.231805Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T09:21:56.230591Z"},"papermill":{"duration":569.456982,"end_time":"2026-09-30T09:21:56.239712+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T09:12:26.78273+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\n","================================================================================\n","PASS A: EXPANDING CHRONOLOGICAL FORWARD VALIDATION (EMBARGOED EVALUATION)\n","================================================================================\n","\n",">>> Variant: REAL (390 features)\n","    Fold 1 (val B2): AP 0.4960 | ROC-AUC 0.8327 | R@0.1%FPR 26.94% | rounds 429\n","             cohorts: new 0.4990 / seen 0.4930 | card overlap 32.0% | ECE_q 0.02859 -> 0.01452\n","    Fold 2 (val B3): AP 0.4759 | ROC-AUC 0.8545 | R@0.1%FPR 24.18% | rounds 142\n","             cohorts: new 0.5404 / seen 0.4485 | card overlap 34.3% | ECE_q 0.00625 -> 0.00642\n","    Fold 3 (val B4): AP 0.5384 | ROC-AUC 0.8912 | R@0.1%FPR 24.08% | rounds 258\n","             cohorts: new 0.5658 / seen 0.5290 | card overlap 41.1% | ECE_q 0.01310 -> 0.00290\n","\n","[5] Internal base-feature-only control — the valid paired comparator for H1.\n","    (Cross-stage comparison against a separate Stage 1 run confounds the\n","     feature set with run configuration; this arm does not.)\n","\n",">>> Variant: BASE_ONLY (371 features)\n","    Fold 1 (val B2): AP 0.5254 | ROC-AUC 0.8674 | R@0.1%FPR 27.80% | rounds 103\n","             cohorts: new 0.5393 / seen 0.5182 | card overlap 32.0% | ECE_q 0.01489 -> 0.01724\n","    Fold 2 (val B3): AP 0.4812 | ROC-AUC 0.8617 | R@0.1%FPR 23.92% | rounds 134\n","             cohorts: new 0.5417 / seen 0.4554 | card overlap 34.3% | ECE_q 0.01253 -> 0.00639\n","    Fold 3 (val B4): AP 0.5330 | ROC-AUC 0.8887 | R@0.1%FPR 25.58% | rounds 179\n","             cohorts: new 0.5657 / seen 0.5193 | card overlap 41.1% | ECE_q 0.00965 -> 0.00243\n","\n","[6] Shuffled-entity null control (N1).\n","\n",">>> Variant: SHUFFLED (390 features)\n","    Fold 1 (val B2): AP 0.4934 | ROC-AUC 0.8298 | R@0.1%FPR 27.02% | rounds 189\n","             cohorts: new 0.4889 / seen 0.4935 | card overlap 32.0% | ECE_q 0.02351 -> 0.01388\n","    Fold 2 (val B3): AP 0.4598 | ROC-AUC 0.8463 | R@0.1%FPR 23.45% | rounds 168\n","             cohorts: new 0.5284 / seen 0.4338 | card overlap 34.3% | ECE_q 0.00602 -> 0.00663\n","    Fold 3 (val B4): AP 0.5194 | ROC-AUC 0.8828 | R@0.1%FPR 24.39% | rounds 221\n","             cohorts: new 0.5449 / seen 0.5088 | card overlap 41.1% | ECE_q 0.01250 -> 0.00228\n","\n","[7] Relational features in isolation (standalone graph signal).\n","\n",">>> Variant: RELATIONAL_ONLY (19 features)\n","    Fold 1 (val B2): AP 0.1492 | ROC-AUC 0.6624 | R@0.1%FPR 4.13% | rounds 154\n","             cohorts: new 0.1000 / seen 0.1707 | card overlap 32.0% | ECE_q 0.02206 -> 0.02017\n","    Fold 2 (val B3): AP 0.2488 | ROC-AUC 0.7666 | R@0.1%FPR 7.39% | rounds 282\n","             cohorts: new 0.2731 / seen 0.2389 | card overlap 34.3% | ECE_q 0.01406 -> 0.00717\n","    Fold 3 (val B4): AP 0.2989 | ROC-AUC 0.8125 | R@0.1%FPR 8.48% | rounds 196\n","             cohorts: new 0.2604 / seen 0.3147 | card overlap 41.1% | ECE_q 0.00771 -> 0.00270\n"]}],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 6. PASS A — Expanding Forward Validation (embargoed, reported metrics)\n","# ==============================================================================\n","folds = [\n","    ([1], 2),\n","    ([1, 2], 3),\n","    ([1, 2, 3], 4),\n","]\n","\n","\n","def run_variant(feature_list: list[str], variant_name: str):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Train and evaluate one experimental arm across expanding forward folds.\n","\n","    Pass A semantics: embargo ON, metrics reported. Returns per-fold records,\n","    the fitted models (reused in Pass B), the round history and gain importance.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    fold_rows: list[dict] = []\n","    models: dict[int, dict] = {}\n","    iters: dict[int, int] = {}\n","    importances: list[pd.DataFrame] = []\n","\n","    print(f\"\\n>>> Variant: {variant_name.upper()} ({len(feature_list)} features)\")\n","\n","    for fold_idx, (train_blocks, val_block) in enumerate(folds, 1):\n","        train_idx = df.index[df[\"chrono_block\"].isin(train_blocks)].to_numpy()\n","        train_max_dt = df.loc[train_idx, CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]].max()\n","\n","        val_all_idx = df.index[df[\"chrono_block\"] == val_block].to_numpy()\n","        val_idx = df.index[\n","            (df[\"chrono_block\"] == val_block)\n","            & (df[CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]] >= train_max_dt + CONFIG[\"EMBARGO_SECONDS\"])\n","        ].to_numpy()\n","\n","        assert not (set(train_idx.tolist()) & OOT_INDEX), \"Fatal: OOT row entered training.\"\n","        assert_causal(df, train_idx, val_idx, f\"{variant_name}_fold{fold_idx}\")\n","\n","        fallback = rounds_from_history(iters, CONFIG[\"FINAL_ROUNDS_RULE\"])\n","        model, best_iter, fit_idx, stop_idx, used_es = train_causal_model(\n","            df, train_idx, feature_list, f\"{variant_name}_fold{fold_idx}\", fallback\n","        )\n","        iters[fold_idx] = best_iter\n","        calibrator = fit_calibrator(model, df, stop_idx, feature_list, best_iter)\n","\n","        X_val = df.loc[val_idx, feature_list]\n","        y_val = df.loc[val_idx, CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"]].values\n","        val_amounts = df.loc[val_idx, CONFIG[\"AMOUNT_COLUMN\"]].values\n","\n","        val_raw = model.predict(X_val, num_iteration=best_iter).astype(np.float32)\n","        val_cal = apply_calibrator(calibrator, val_raw)\n","\n","        models[fold_idx] = {\n","            \"model\": model, \"best_iter\": best_iter, \"calibrator\": calibrator,\n","            \"train_idx\": train_idx, \"val_block\": val_block,\n","        }\n","\n","        m_raw = compute_metrics(y_val, val_raw, val_amounts)\n","        m_cal = compute_metrics(y_val, val_cal, val_amounts)\n","\n","        first_seen_val = df.loc[val_idx, \"card_first_seen\"].to_numpy()\n","        ap_new = (average_precision_score(y_val[first_seen_val], val_raw[first_seen_val])\n","                  if y_val[first_seen_val].sum() > 0 else np.nan)\n","        ap_seen = (average_precision_score(y_val[~first_seen_val], val_raw[~first_seen_val])\n","                   if y_val[~first_seen_val].sum() > 0 else np.nan)\n","\n","        card_overlap = entity_overlap_rate(df, train_idx, val_idx, \"uid_card\")\n","        device_overlap = entity_overlap_rate(df, train_idx, val_idx, \"uid_device\")\n","\n","        importances.append(pd.DataFrame({\n","            \"feature\": model.feature_name(),\n","            f\"gain_fold{fold_idx}\": model.feature_importance(\"gain\"),\n","        }).set_index(\"feature\"))\n","\n","        fold_rows.append({\n","            \"variant\": variant_name,\n","            \"fold\": fold_idx,\n","            \"train_blocks\": str(train_blocks),\n","            \"val_block\": val_block,\n","            \"n_features\": len(feature_list),\n","            \"n_fit\": int(len(fit_idx)),\n","            \"n_stop\": int(len(stop_idx)),\n","            \"n_val\": int(len(val_idx)),\n","            \"n_val_embargoed_out\": int(len(val_all_idx) - len(val_idx)),\n","            \"best_iter\": best_iter,\n","            \"early_stopped\": bool(used_es),\n","            \"val_fraud_rate\": float(y_val.mean()),\n","            \"AP_new_entity\": ap_new,\n","            \"AP_seen_entity\": ap_seen,\n","            \"first_seen_share\": float(first_seen_val.mean()),\n","            \"card_overlap_rate\": card_overlap,\n","            \"device_overlap_rate\": device_overlap,\n","            \"AP_calibrated\": m_cal[\"AP\"],\n","            \"ECE_calibrated\": m_cal[\"ECE\"],\n","            \"ECE_quantile_calibrated\": m_cal[\"ECE_quantile\"],\n","            \"Brier_calibrated\": m_cal[\"Brier\"],\n","            \"Loss_cost_rule_calibrated\": m_cal[\"Loss_cost_rule\"],\n","            \"AlertRate_calibrated\": m_cal[\"AlertRate\"],\n","            **m_raw,\n","        })\n","\n","        print(f\"    Fold {fold_idx} (val B{val_block}): AP {m_raw['AP']:.4f} | \"\n","              f\"ROC-AUC {m_raw['ROC_AUC']:.4f} | R@0.1%FPR {m_raw['Recall@0.1%FPR']:.2%} | \"\n","              f\"rounds {best_iter}{'' if used_es else ' (fixed)'}\")\n","        print(f\"             cohorts: new {ap_new:.4f} / seen {ap_seen:.4f} \"\n","              f\"| card overlap {card_overlap:.1%} | ECE_q {m_raw['ECE_quantile']:.5f} \"\n","              f\"-> {m_cal['ECE_quantile']:.5f}\")\n","\n","    imp_df = pd.concat(importances, axis=1).fillna(0.0)\n","    return pd.DataFrame(fold_rows), models, iters, imp_df\n","\n","\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n","print(\"PASS A: EXPANDING CHRONOLOGICAL FORWARD VALIDATION (EMBARGOED EVALUATION)\")\n","print(\"=\" * 80)\n","\n","real_results, real_models, real_iters, real_importance = run_variant(stage2_features, \"real\")\n","\n","if CONFIG[\"RUN_BASE_ONLY\"]:\n","    print(\"\\n[5] Internal base-feature-only control — the valid paired comparator for H1.\")\n","    print(\"    (Cross-stage comparison against a separate Stage 1 run confounds the\")\n","    print(\"     feature set with run configuration; this arm does not.)\")\n","    base_results, base_models, base_iters, base_importance = run_variant(base_features, \"base_only\")\n","else:\n","    base_results, base_models, base_iters, base_importance = pd.DataFrame(), {}, {}, pd.DataFrame()\n","\n","if CONFIG[\"RUN_SHUFFLE_CONTROL\"]:\n","    print(\"\\n[6] Shuffled-entity null control (N1).\")\n","    control_results, control_models, control_iters, _ = run_variant(control_features, \"shuffled\")\n","else:\n","    control_results, control_models, control_iters = pd.DataFrame(), {}, {}\n","\n","if CONFIG[\"RUN_RELATIONAL_ONLY\"]:\n","    print(\"\\n[7] Relational features in isolation (standalone graph signal).\")\n","    rel_only_results, rel_only_models, rel_only_iters, _ = run_variant(relational_cols, \"relational_only\")\n","else:\n","    rel_only_results, rel_only_models, rel_only_iters = pd.DataFrame(), {}, {}"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":9,"id":"7eeea5c7","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T09:21:56.25416Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T09:21:56.253774Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T09:21:56.288912Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T09:21:56.287966Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.045217,"end_time":"2026-09-30T09:21:56.291188+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T09:21:56.245971+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\n","[8] Auditing cross-fold feature-importance stability (real arm)...\n","    Spearman rank correlation of gain importance across folds:\n","            gain_fold1  gain_fold2  gain_fold3\n","gain_fold1      1.0000      0.8916      0.8624\n","gain_fold2      0.8916      1.0000      0.9095\n","gain_fold3      0.8624      0.9095      1.0000\n","    Relational share of total gain: 29.8% (19/390 = 4.9% of columns)\n","    Top-10 by mean gain: V258, C1, P_emaildomain_seen_before, card2_seen_before, card1_seen_before, C13, C14, addr1_seen_before, D2, uid_device_seen_before\n","    Saved: ./artifacts/stage2_feature_importance.csv\n"]}],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 7. Feature-Importance Stability Audit\n","# ==============================================================================\n","print(\"\\n[8] Auditing cross-fold feature-importance stability (real arm)...\")\n","gain_cols = [c for c in real_importance.columns if c.startswith(\"gain_\")]\n","gain_ranks = real_importance[gain_cols].rank(ascending=False)\n","rank_corr = gain_ranks.corr(method=\"spearman\")\n","\n","real_importance[\"gain_mean\"] = real_importance[gain_cols].mean(axis=1)\n","real_importance[\"gain_cv\"] = (\n","    real_importance[gain_cols].std(axis=1)\n","    / real_importance[gain_cols].mean(axis=1).replace(0, np.nan)\n",")\n","real_importance[\"is_relational\"] = real_importance.index.isin(relational_cols)\n","real_importance = real_importance.sort_values(\"gain_mean\", ascending=False)\n","\n","total_gain = real_importance[\"gain_mean\"].sum()\n","rel_gain_share = float(\n","    real_importance.loc[real_importance[\"is_relational\"], \"gain_mean\"].sum()\n","    / max(total_gain, 1e-9)\n",")\n","\n","importance_path = os.path.join(CONFIG[\"OUTPUT_DIR\"], \"stage2_feature_importance.csv\")\n","real_importance.to_csv(importance_path)\n","\n","print(\"    Spearman rank correlation of gain importance across folds:\")\n","print(rank_corr.round(4).to_string())\n","print(f\"    Relational share of total gain: {rel_gain_share:.1%} \"\n","      f\"({len(relational_cols)}/{len(stage2_features)} = \"\n","      f\"{len(relational_cols) / len(stage2_features):.1%} of columns)\")\n","print(f\"    Top-10 by mean gain: {', '.join(real_importance.index[:10].tolist())}\")\n","print(f\"    Saved: {importance_path}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"id":"def31f49","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T09:21:56.305738Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T09:21:56.305044Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T09:27:19.826383Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09